	I've been playing wizards for sometime now and most of the comments
made in the previous postings are what I've seen. 
	However, once you get a couple of items, it becomes a lot easier.
From my experience, what is needed, is a good weapon, like a longsword which
can be converted to Excalibur, and Gauntlets of power. Every time I've got
these two in the first four levels (mainly in shops) I have had pretty long
games, only to die from things like choking over food!! (trying for intrinsics)
Also, reverse genociding wraiths really helps. With high Int., spellbooks
are extremely useful.
	Another useful intrinsic to get is the teleporting intrinsic (from
leprechauns etc.). Once you reach the higher levels, where you meet giants
dragons etc. teleporting uses up a lot of energy  in one move and you 
become hungry before the next monster corpse rots, by teleporting several
times in succession.
	In my best game so far, I got the amulet, got upto the castle level
and forgot to put on the ring of levitation!! Ouch!! I am not likely to 
forget that again! 


